-var-create: deque — value, type, displayhint array, flat .[i] children
-var-create: empty deque — 'with 0 elements', has_more 0, no children
-var-create: empty list — 'empty std::__cxx11::list' (not 'with 0 elements'), has_more 0
-var-create: list — value/type carry the __cxx11 tag, no count, no displayhint at all
-var-create: map — value/type/children (flat alternating key,value, numchild 2×N) match real GDB exactly
-var-create: priority_queue — value/type match real GDB, displayhint array; children are OUR priority-drain order, not GDB's raw heap array (documented divergence)
-var-create: queue — 'wrapping: std::deque with N elements', children front-to-back (push order)
-var-create: set — value/type/children match real GDB exactly, NO displayhint (like list)
-var-create: singular 'element' for a 1-element container
-var-create: stack — 'wrapping: std::deque with N elements', children bottom-to-top (push order)
-var-update: growth after push_back/push/pop is reflected (numchild via var-list-children, value text, no crash)
-var-update: priority_queue/set/map growth after push/insert/[]= is reflected (new_num_children, values)
